window.EN={"1":"The western isles currently where Roy and the others are—","2":"Fibernia.","3":"Caledonia, to the south.","4":"And Dia, to the northeast.","5":"This is what those three islands together are called.","6":"Every one of the islands has rich mineral veins, and mining had been carried out vigorously.","7":"Of them, the largest could be said to be Mount Eburacum, at the northern tip of the island of Fibernia.","8":"Seeking information on the \"bandits,\" Roy and the others decided to set their course north, aiming for it.","9":"They were told that to reach Mount Eburacum, they would have to pass through a castle in the mountains.","10":"Roy sent a messenger to request passage from Nord, the lord of that castle.","11":"Since they themselves had come to this island at Etruria's formal request—","12":"Surely getting his cooperation would be easy...","13":"It did not take long for them to realize how wrong that assumption was...","14":"(Nord): Hey, what happened to that spy from the resistance?","15":"(Soldier): The dancer, you mean, the one called Larum? She's been thrown in the dungeon for now.","16":"(Nord): So? Did she say anything?","17":"(Soldier): Well... she just keeps repeating that it's some kind of mistake.","18":"(Nord): Hmph. And she thinks that'll talk her way out of it?","19":"(Nord): If it comes to that, I'll question her myself...","20":"(Soldier): Lord Nord.","21":"(Nord): What is it?","22":"(Soldier): A messenger has arrived from the Lycian Alliance army.","23":"(Nord): Oh? The ones supposedly sent out to put down those \"bandits\"?","24":"(Soldier): They're requesting permission to pass through this castle on their way to the northern mine.","25":"(Nord): ...The Lycian Alliance army, is it.","26":"(Nord): Governor-General Alcard of the Western Isles gave an order—","27":"(Nord): that while they're here in Fibernia, we're to find a suitable excuse and dispose of them... kukuku.","28":"(Nord): A perfect chance to curry favor with Lord Alcard.","29":"(Nord): Right! Send out the troops and have them attacked!!","30":"(Soldier): Yes sir.","31":"(Soldier): What should we do about the messenger?","32":"(Nord): Dispose of him.","33":"(Soldier): Yes sir, understood.","34":"(Nord): And don't forget to station the archers at the Shooter!!","35":"(Nord): That's an excellent weapon that can strike from far away— use it to throw their movements into confusion!","36":"(Soldier): Yes sir.","37":"(Nord): Whatever you do, don't let the enemy seize it!!","38":"(Marinus): Lord Roy! Soldiers have come out from the castle!!","39":"(Roy): What!? Are there \"bandits\" around here too, perhaps?","40":"(Marinus): No, however you look at it, it seems they're after us","41":"(Roy): ...What about the messenger we sent?","42":"(Marinus): It's been quite a while now, and he hasn't come back... which means...","43":"(Roy): What do you mean?","44":"(Roy): Why would the lord of this castle attack us?","45":"(Marinus): Th-the enemy's gotten that close already... Lord Roy, what should we do?","46":"(Roy): ...There's nothing for it but to fight back.","47":"(Roy): In any case, let's head for the castle— we might learn something there.","48":"(Marinus): I see... yes, quite so.","49":"(Roy): All right, everyone, let's break through here!","50":"(Roy): But please, avoid any unnecessary fighting if you can.","51":"(Villager): Mr. Guese, are you really going?","52":"(Guese): Yeah. My men's killers are in that castle.","53":"(Guese): I can't just let that go.","54":"(Villager): The ones who were always with you, you mean?","55":"(Guese): Yeah. While I was away, under the pretext of some job from the Etrurian governor's office—","56":"(Guese): they were taken off and worked half to death in the mine, and in the end, every one of them...","57":"(Villager): ......","58":"(Guese): They were all idiots, but every one of them was a good man.","59":"(Guese): And they went and did that to them...!!","60":"(Villager): So, Mr. Guese, you're going to take revenge all on your own?","61":"(Guese): Is that strange?","62":"(Villager): It's not that, but... are you really not going back to shipping anymore?","63":"(Guese): Well, that...","64":"(Guese): Once I've avenged them, if the fighting's died down, I'll think about it.","65":"(Villager): I see... we won't forget it, you know.","66":"(Villager): That even braving the dangers of the sea, you carried and sold all kinds of things for us.","67":"(Villager): If anything ever happens, you can always come rely on us.","68":"(Guese): If I'm still alive, sure. Thanks, auntie.","69":"(Nord): Gonzalez! Is Gonzalez here!","70":"(Gonzalez): I... I'm here...","71":"(Nord): A little to the north, along the mountains, there's a village. You know the one.","72":"(Gonzalez): I know it.","73":"(Nord): It might be a hideout for those resistance types.","74":"(Nord): Go, and crush the whole village.","75":"(Gonzalez): The whole village...","76":"(Nord): That's right. Hurry, don't dawdle!","77":"(Nord): A good-for-nothing wretch like you is only of use at a time like this, after all.","78":"(Gonzalez): I... I...","79":"(Nord): What, do you have a complaint?","80":"(Gonzalez): No... I don't...","81":"(Nord): Hmph. For all that face of yours, you can be strangely soft at times.","82":"(Nord): You'd think crushing a single village would be nothing to you.","83":"(Guese): Hm? What, you want something from me?","84":"(Roy): No, it's just— I was concerned, seeing you fighting the castle's soldiers alone.","85":"(Guese): And who are you?","86":"(Roy): I'm Roy. I lead the Lycian Alliance army.","87":"(Roy): We came here at Etruria's request.","88":"(Guese): A lackey of Etruria's, huh! Then you're an enemy— get ready!!","89":"(Roy): W-wait, please!","90":"(Roy): We're fighting the castle's soldiers too.","91":"(Guese): ? What do you mean?","92":"(Roy): To be honest, we don't understand the reason ourselves either...","93":"(Roy): We're just acting to carry out our mission of putting down the \"bandits,\" but...","94":"(Guese): ...You said you're fighting those castle men.","95":"(Guese): Then how about hiring me?","96":"(Roy): Huh?","97":"(Guese): I'm a pirate, see, so I know this area pretty well.","98":"(Guese): Looks like you lot just got to this island.","99":"(Guese): Don't you need someone to show you around?","100":"(Roy): That would be reassuring, but why the sudden offer?","101":"(Guese): I want to help hunt down these \"bandits.\"","102":"(Guese): Well, truth be told, I suppose I'd get lumped in as one too, being a pirate myself.","103":"(Roy): In that case, please, we'd be grateful.","104":"(Guese): Fine, leave it to me.","105":"(Guese): ...Hang on, my brothers of the sea. I'll avenge you for sure!","106":"(Guese): What happens after that depends on that Roy fellow, I suppose.","107":"(Larum): U-um, excuse me!","108":"(Gonzalez): Wh-what do you want... I'm the enemy, you know!","109":"(Larum): I'm sorry, suddenly talking to you like this.","110":"(Larum): But your eyes looked so sad...","111":"(Gonzalez): ...You... do you know... there's a village... along the mountains?","112":"(Larum): Yes, I know it.","113":"(Gonzalez): Get the people there... to run.","114":"(Gonzalez): I... got orders... go crush the village... so...","115":"(Larum): No, stop it! The village people haven't done anything wrong...","116":"(Gonzalez): No good... orders are absolute... I... can't disobey.","117":"(Larum): Can't you get away from the people who give orders like that?","118":"(Gonzalez): Get away?","119":"(Larum): That's it! Come fight together with us!","120":"(Larum): You could protect the people of this island.","121":"(Gonzalez): ...No good... I... am a monster... no one... can be with me.","122":"(Gonzalez): The village I was born in... everyone... threw stones at me.","123":"(Gonzalez): Told me... to leave the village... I'm a monster... not human.","124":"(Larum): That's not true! You're a human being— you're a good person, I can tell!","125":"(Larum): Come on, let's go together... don't be afraid.","126":"(Gonzalez): Afraid... me?","127":"(Gonzalez): I'm... not afraid... I'm not afraid of anything...","128":"(Gonzalez): Everyone... is afraid of me... ...I'm not afraid!","129":"(Larum): No, you are afraid.","130":"(Larum): Afraid that they'll throw stones at you again.","131":"(Larum): Afraid that you'll be driven out again.","132":"(Larum): Just like a little bird trembling in its nest.","133":"(Gonzalez): ......","134":"(Larum): No one in our army will discriminate against you.","135":"(Larum): Come now, be brave and take one step forward— to live looking ahead...","136":"(Villager): I wonder if little Larum is safe... I'm worried.","137":"(Villager): And all because she brought us these weapons...","138":"(Villager): We told her to stay hidden, but with that personality of hers...","139":"(Villager): This axe too, you know, it's one she brought us.","140":"(Villager): It's supposed to be a strange axe, strong against swords but weak against lances.","141":"(Villager): More than something like this, I'd rather see that girl's dancing again...","142":"(Villager): \"Obtained the Sword Buster.\"","143":"(Villager): Mountain bandits and pirates too, when they were born, were once cute little babies.","144":"(Villager): If you speak to them with sincerity, I want to believe they'll understand... though...","145":"(Nord, battle intro): Kukuku, so you've come.","146":"(Nord, battle intro): I'll take it, then... your life energy.","147":"(Nord, defeated): I... I'm dying...","148":"(Nord, defeated): My life... is draining away...","149":"(Marinus): Lord Roy...","150":"(Marinus): In the end, we never did learn the reason these men attacked our army.","151":"(Roy): But between that ambush before, and this attack now...","152":"(Roy): It seems certain someone is targeting us.","153":"(Roy): Hmm, perhaps we ought to send an inquiry to the Etrurian royal palace about this.","154":"(Roy): Yes, that's right— this is no time to be worrying about hunting down \"bandits\"...","155":"(Roy): In any case, let's consult General Cecilia about this first.","156":"(Soldier): Excuse me.","157":"(Soldier): There's a girl who was being held in this castle's dungeon who says she has something she wants to tell Lord Roy...","158":"(Roy): Me? I wonder what it could be— bring her here, please.","159":"(Soldier): Yes sir.","160":"(Larum): Are you Lord Roy? The one who's come to hunt down the \"bandits\"...?","161":"(Roy): Yes, that's right.","162":"(Larum): Lord Roy, please! Save my friends— save them!!","163":"(Roy): Whoa!","164":"(Marinus): Now then, girl! Get away from Lord Roy!","165":"(Roy): N-now, let's all just calm down and talk.","166":"(Roy): These friends of yours, who are they?","167":"(Larum): I'm Larum. I'm one of this island's resistance fighters.","168":"(Roy): The group that fights the \"bandits\" and protects the islanders' way of life, right?","169":"(Larum): Yeah... no, wait!","170":"(Roy): It's not that?","171":"(Larum): Of course we do that too, but, our real enemies are—","172":"(Larum): the lords who came from Etruria, who shelter the \"bandits\" and use them as a cover!","173":"(Roy): What did you say! Is that really true!?","174":"(Larum): The lords here forcibly take everyone on the island off to the mines,","175":"(Larum): and make them work there until they die!!","176":"(Larum): Even if they're hurt, even if they get sick, they're never, ever allowed to rest from work...","177":"(Roy): ...Something that terrible is happening...","178":"(Larum): That's why! We're fighting all over the island!!","179":"(Larum): This time too, we were supposed to go to Mount Eburacum to the north and save the people there, but...!!","180":"(Roy): What's wrong? Calm down!","181":"(Larum): It seems like our plan got found out! The villager there was so terrified...","182":"(Larum): But I never imagined he'd actually talk...","183":"(Larum): If we don't warn them quickly, everyone... Lady Echidna...!!","184":"(Roy): Understood— let's head for the northern mine at once!","185":"(Roy): To save the resistance and the people being forced to work in the mine.","186":"(Larum): Really!? I'm so happy— thank you, Lord Roy!!","187":"(Roy): Whoa! H-hey, wait a moment, Miss Larum—","188":"(Marinus): Now then, girl! Didn't I tell you to get away from Lord Roy!","189":"(Larum): Lord Roy, here! Use this!","190":"(Roy): This sword is...?","191":"(Larum): I was keeping it in trust— our leader Lady Echidna's sword.","192":"(Larum): Since you're going to help the resistance,","193":"(Larum): I don't think Lady Echidna would mind you all using it.","194":"(Larum): It's called the \"Dragon Killer,\" but since dragons don't really exist anymore...","195":"(Larum): I wonder if it just means it's strong against dragon knights or something? I don't really get it myself."};
